<p align="left"><br>
The Illinois-Missouri Indoor Bullseye Pistol League was
established in 1949. The wise men who founded our organization
are:</p>

<p align="center">Max Thompson<br>
Frank Novak<br>
Herman Bockstruck<br>
Frank Stubits</p>

<p align="left">In the late forties, there were several shooting
teams participating in outdoor matches during the summer in the
bi-state area. In 1949, employees of the Winchester-Western
company thought it would be good idea to organize an indoor
winter league to keep everyone sharp over the off-season. Indeed
it was! Thus the &quot;Ill-Mo Pistol League&quot; was born. The
original teams that participated in that very first season were:</p>

<p align="center">Winchester-Western<br>
Industrial Pistol Club<br>
St. Louis Police<br>
Piasa Pistol Club<br>
St. Louis Revolver Club<br>
Small Arms Armory Team</p>

<p align="center">(A complete historiography of our organization,
complete with photographs and interviews, is being researched and
developed. Check back often as information will be added as it is
available.)</p>

<p align="center">&nbsp;</p>
